# Write a service

Trellis projects explicitly list `.trellis` files under `[sources]`. The compiler
resolves native source-package semantics and generates private TypeScript or Rust
packages.

1. [Set up the project](/guides/write-a-service/setup)
2. [Declare the API and participant](/guides/write-a-service/first-contract)
3. [Connect the generated service](/guides/write-a-service/service-entrypoint)
4. [Install source packages and generate SDKs](/guides/write-a-service/contract-artifacts)
5. [Use the development loop](/guides/write-a-service/development-loop)

6. [Call it in a real-runtime test](/guides/testing-trellis-services)

This walkthrough implements one RPC end to end. The operations, jobs, State, and
store guides expand those features independently; it is not a complete IDL
grammar reference. Deno, environment variables, and UUIDs are demonstration
choices, not Trellis requirements.
